1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Who shares patients with Dr. A?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Source tables sit
in Unity Catalog.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,500
One path copies data out.
One starts warehouse SQL.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:18,300
Spark SQL builds the graph.

5
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:22,100
Keys become nodes and edges

6
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:26,000
Patients fold. Under 11 none

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,200
sum of step run times
preflight to switch

8
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:36,160
Kit v1: a full copy each build.
Lakebase can also sync
changes only.

9
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:41,400
The whole walk is one SQL
statement. Each hop is one CTE.

10
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:47,500
Two routes, one row.
Cut keeps 25 per hop.

11
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:53,800
The walk adds hop 3 and hop 4
the same way.

12
00:00:53,800 --> 00:01:01,500
client p95 · warm · in-region
prepared statements off · 4 CU

13
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:04,700
The same kit walks a tree.

14
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:10,500
From diabetes mellitus,
one loop adds one is-a level.

15
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:15,500
A rebuild is a new version.

16
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:20,500
Timing graph: 20 seeds equal
a source-table reference.

17
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:26,240
Graph databases still win
for ad hoc traversals
of unknown length

18
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:30,600
github.com/saselvan/
graph-kit-for-lakebase
